Some appearances work fully, some show visual or animation issues, and unsupported looks fall back to Genessa's original double. NPC/enemy compatibility improvements are planned separately.

[b]F.A.Q.[/b]

[b]Does it copy my CSS customization?[/b]
Yes, for supported appearances. Doubles follow your current CSS look, including supported colors, body settings, shown/hidden parts, fabric and glow. You do not need to save a profile first.

[b]Which outfits have been tested?[/b]
Unholy Genessa, Eve and Commander White, in both Faithful and Stray forms. Other outfits depend on compatible materials and skeletons; being a CSS mod alone does not guarantee support.

[b]What if I use CCS?[/b]
CSS controls appearance; CCS controls your combat setup. The doubles keep the game's normal attack-copying behavior, so supported copied attacks can reflect your CCS setup. This does not apply every CCS setting directly to each double.

[b]Do I need to update my outfit mods?[/b]
No update is needed for the tested Unholy Genessa, Eve or Commander White packages. Install CSS beta.11 and its separate Astral Shared Assets download. Keep the older CSS_SharedAssets_P Eve package if you have it.

[b]Can I keep the original doubles?[/b]
Yes. Set Faithful Doubles or Stray Doubles to Default in MISC. Each choice is independent.

[b]Can another gameplay shell use this ability?[/b]
No. Your actual gameplay shell must be Genessa. Wearing her appearance alone does not grant her abilities.

Close the game, extract the runtime ZIP into [b]MortalShell2/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods/[/b] and overwrite. Keep your [b]CustomShellSystem/state/[/b] folder.
